    "I've spent the better part of two decades watching brand guidelines gather dust on shelves. Beautifully designed PDFs that no one opens after the first week. The problem isn't that guidelines are wrong -- it's that they're incomplete. They tell you what not to do. They don't tell you how to think.",
    "A brand system is fundamentally different. Where guidelines are a rulebook, a system is a toolkit. It gives your team the building blocks -- color, type, spacing, imagery, tone -- and the logic for combining them. It's the difference between handing someone a recipe and teaching them how to cook.",
