    "Guidelines break at the edges. Systems flex. When we rebuilt GLG's visual language, we didn't write more rules. We built a flexible grid, a rationalized color system, and a typography hierarchy that could adapt from pitch decks to product interfaces. Every element earned its place because it solved a recurring problem, not because it looked good in a PDF.",
    "The test of a brand system is what happens when you're not in the room. If the design team in another office, on another continent, can produce work that feels unmistakably on-brand without calling you -- the system is working. If they can't, you don't have a system. You have a style guide and a bottleneck.",
    "The brands that endure -- the ones that feel coherent across every touchpoint -- aren't the ones with the thickest guidelines. They're the ones with the clearest systems. Systems that trust the people using them. Systems that answer 'how' instead of just 'don't.'",
